{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">VL82 is a Soviet twin-section freight dual-system electric locomotive. It is designed for non-stop train operation on sections electrified with both 25 kV 50 Hz AC and 3 kV DC. It was developed based on the eight-axle electric locomotives VL10 and VL80.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Dual-system electric locomotives are used on railway mainlines where transitions exist between sections electrified with AC and DC (neutral sections), but where constructing a dedicated transition station is unfeasible for various reasons. At the same time, dual-system locomotives, utilizing full power in both modes, have increased weight (which is not a disadvantage for freight locomotives) and higher costs for electrical equipment and its maintenance.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Starting in 1972, the factory began producing an improved version of the dual-system locomotive, designated VL82M. A total of 67 such locomotives were built by 1979.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Compared to their predecessors, the new locomotives feature a redesigned body structure (instead of single large round headlights on the front, they have twin headlights with visors, similar to the VL80T, and modified side panels), along with other improvements.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3614870?t=1743678726","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3614870?t=1743678726","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3614870/3b0d3fac6321cdcc4484f2c8cc6a87b81c3a14e0/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1743678726","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3614870/3b0d3fac6321cdcc4484f2c8cc6a87b81c3a14e0/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1743678726","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Downloadable Content","id":21},{"description":"Includes level editor","id":17}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">VL82 is a Soviet twin-section freight dual-system electric locomotive. It is designed for non-stop train operation on sections electrified with both 25 kV 50 Hz AC and 3 kV DC. It was developed based on the eight-axle electric locomotives VL10 and VL80.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Dual-system electric locomotives are used on railway mainlines where transitions exist between sections electrified with AC and DC (neutral sections), but where constructing a dedicated transition station is unfeasible for various reasons. At the same time, dual-system locomotives, utilizing full power in both modes, have increased weight (which is not a disadvantage for freight locomotives) and higher costs for electrical equipment and its maintenance.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Starting in 1972, the factory began producing an improved version of the dual-system locomotive, designated VL82M. A total of 67 such locomotives were built by 1979.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Compared to their predecessors, the new locomotives feature a redesigned body structure (instead of single large round headlights on the front, they have twin headlights with visors, similar to the VL80T, and modified side panels), along with other improvements.</p>","developers":["ZDSimulator Team"],"fullgame":{"appid":"3381120","name":"ZDSimulator"},"genres":[{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3614870/27a8315e347eb3edeb18e5aae50e33565292e5aa/header.jpg?t=1743678726","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"name":"ZDSimulator - VL82 Locomotive","package_groups":[],"pc_requirements":[],"platforms":{"linux":false,"mac":false,"windows":true},"publishers":["ZDSimulator Team"],"ratings":{"dejus":{"banned":"0","descriptors":"","rating":"l","rating_generated":"1","required_age":"0","use_age_gate":"0"},"steam_germany":{"banned":"0","descriptors":"","r